-- Scale status: hold.
-- Public outreach and acquisition scaling remain gated on iOS crash diagnosis, complete exact-build physical-device and internal-delivery coverage, and critical console guardrails. The protected hosted full-byte repeat now passes; the mutable draft must still be rechecked by that chain before every later use. Open-Meteo written clearance passes for the exact unpaid, non-monetized organic-promotion scope, and the exact source-current signed artifact set remains atomically verified-current in the still draft-blocked upload manifest.
-- Scale gates are fail-closed. Unknown is not treated as pass.
SELECT *
FROM (
  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect reports two crashes for public iOS 1.0.1 (4): one on 2026-08-25 and one on 2026-08-29. The 2026-08-29 event maps to iPhone; the 2026-08-25 device/OS dimension is suppressed or unavailable. Neither event exposes a diagnostic, stack, incident/signature ID, or crashed-binary UUID. Current product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 inherits preventive storage-failure hardening and tolerant optional Open-Meteo decoding; ordinary exact-source run 33300967788 passed shared Simulator tests and 18/18 Apple surface-state tests. Protected run 33381050098 provides the independently byte-verified distribution-signed 1.1.0 (6) IPA/archive with matching profiles, entitlements, signatures, and dSYM UUIDs. That exact IPA was delivered through Transporter and App Store Connect now reports build 6 as VALID and APP_STORE_ELIGIBLE. It is not the crashed public build, has not been installed through TestFlight, and cannot identify or be attributed to either production event. Diagnostic access and symbolication, TestFlight beta-group distribution, an exact physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing.', 'Obtain and symbolicate any diagnostic Apple exposes, confirm TestFlight beta-group distribution for processed build 6, complete the iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'pass', 'Product/build-input commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). Exact-source ordinary GitHub Actions run 33300967788 passed Android/shared, Apple, and all 15 Compose UI tests across API 24 phone, API 36 phone, and API 36 tablet. Protected signing run 33381050098 produced the schema-v3 receipt-bound source-current set. Hosted materialization run 33392732428 retained the exact package and receipt in unpublished mutable draft release 379745439. A fresh local macOS verification reopened all 104 safely extracted files with pinned Bundletool 1.18.3. Protected workflow_run 33405849102 completed isolated no-checkout staging and the separate read-only hosted macOS verifier, returning byte_verified=true for phone d4a90676f32745ea314b50ced2c9955e86923589534a1a7654ac6f1207e88a62, Wear e76d685b20e86f8878be7c9a1a59ac6edb5781ec8e61d5ecd36feb52ddc1cccf, and Apple 7466afb1a06f3000ad5d095734082d57cf58e992bdd7a8bed326e90d26ba39d0. The committed manifest remains atomically 3/3 verified-current and draft-blocked because physical QA is separate. The draft remains mutable, so the protected chain must recheck it before every later use. Those exact bytes were subsequently accepted into the separate phone and Wear Play Internal tracks, while Apple build 6 completed processing as VALID and APP_STORE_ELIGIBLE; see growth/quality/internal-store-delivery-2026-08-31.md. No physical-device runtime pass follows from store acceptance, and no TestFlight beta install, Play-delivered install, production review/rollout, public availability, crash-gate closure, or ranking claim is made.', 'Require the protected hosted chain to recheck the mutable draft before every later use, then bind store-delivered physical QA without changing the promoted artifact bytes'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 retains independently byte-verified upload-key-signed phone AAB d4a90676f32745ea314b50ced2c9955e86923589534a1a7654ac6f1207e88a62 and Wear AAB e76d685b20e86f8878be7c9a1a59ac6edb5781ec8e61d5ecd36feb52ddc1cccf. On 2026-08-31 the exact phone AAB was reopened with pinned Bundletool 1.18.3 and converted without rebuilding into universal APK e970352d54e4c95100f03539c54dbecb0732c635e2f6057715215f271d24e976. A clean physical General Mobile Android 7.1.1 / API 25 install reproduced the pulled base.apk hash and passed Russian onboarding without location, live Tashkent forecast, Best Time Outside, native share chooser, proven-offline cache/fallback, recovery, and process-health checks. The same exact AAB is now available on Play Internal track 4700083514281298386 with the existing four-account License testers group; the device opens the invite, but it has not been accepted and no Play-delivered install exists. Exact Wear 1.1.0 (1000008) is available on Internal track 4699242452771231163, but that track is inactive because it has zero tester groups and no Wear install exists. Play-delivered phone rerun, physical tablet/widget coverage, paired physical Wear OS coverage, and post-delivery vitals remain missing. The Samsung API 36 device still contains user data and is not overwritten. Production was not changed. The gate remains blocked.', 'Complete authorized tester access, accept the phone invite, rerun the phone scope against the Play-delivered package, and complete physical tablet/widget and paired Wear OS QA'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains simulator-only Apple evidence that does not transfer to current authority 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652. Twelve targeted current-source iOS Simulator provider tests and exact-source hosted Apple regression tests pass. Protected run 33381050098 provides independently byte-verified distribution-signed IPA 7466afb1a06f3000ad5d095734082d57cf58e992bdd7a8bed326e90d26ba39d0 plus matching xcarchive, app/widget/watch profiles, entitlements, signatures, and dSYM UUIDs for 1.1.0 (6), and trusted hosted run 33405849102 repeated the full verifier successfully. The exact IPA completed Transporter delivery; App Store Connect build 6 is VALID, APP_STORE_ELIGIBLE, not expired, and declares iOS 15.0 minimum. Direct devicectl installation remains invalid because the IPA uses App Store profiles, so exact runtime proof must use TestFlight. The iPhone 14 Pro on iOS 26.6.1 and iPad mini 5 on iPadOS 26.6 are paired, booted, Developer Mode enabled, and suitable for a TestFlight update and fresh install. The paired Series 5 watch on watchOS 10.6.2 is compatible, but Developer Mode is disabled and its developer tunnel is disconnected. No iOS 15 runtime is locally available. TestFlight beta-group distribution/install, the physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing. The gate remains blocked.', 'Confirm TestFlight beta-group distribution for processed build 6, install it on the ready iPhone and iPad, restore watch readiness, then run the complete iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. An authenticated read-only recheck at 2026-08-31 23:17–23:23 +05:00 confirmed that review request 14 contains only the Uzbekistan Custom Store Listing en-US and ru-RU store data and is На рассмотрении. Managed publishing is off and the latest verified publication remains 2026-08-27. This proves review submission, not approval, publication, propagation, or a later policy guarantee. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md, growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md, and growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-31.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
) AS gates(gate_id, gate, status, evidence, next_action);
